\"287.9\" y2=\"287.9\" stroke=\"#A63A2E\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"291.9\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#A63A2E\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$583.80</tspan> Nov 5 low</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"232.5\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These lines are mine, not yours: the Nov 5 low, the 200-day average, and my 38.2% and 50% retracements of the drop from the Sept 24 high ($779.82) to the Nov 5 low ($583.80).</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> mixed, tilting down. Price $628.77 is under the 20-day ($646.10) and the 50-day ($678.45), and closed $1.94 under the 200-day ($630.71) after two closes above it. The 50-day is still above the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 43.4, soft. The stock is 19% under its 52-week high.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> $648.45, where the last three days' highs stopped, right at the 20-day. Then my 38.2% line at $658.68 and my 50% line at $681.81, next to the 50-day.</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> $583.80 (Nov 5 low). Under it, the July–August lows ($524–537) and the 52-week low at $519.37.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> does not apply today. Price is under the 200-day and RSI is above 40. If price gets back over the 200-day and RSI dips under 40, it would.</li><li><strong>Scorecard:</strong> no open or watching play.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports neither side yet. It disagrees with the strength management described in ads; the drop began the day after the report, when the legal charge and the New Mexico order landed together. A close above $658.68 would lean it up; a close below $583.80 would lean it down.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The next report (date not found, likely late January): 2027 expense and capital spending figures, and any new legal accrual.</li><li>Court dates: the New Mexico appeal filings, approval of the state agreement, and the February 2027 school-district trials.</li><li>Jan 19, 2027: the Class C charter change, and any share sale that follows.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results, guidance and commitments (company release, company transcript, 10-Q). Thin: the New Mexico penalty's terms come from the 10-Q plus third-party press; outlets differ on the size of the state agreement (PYMNTS reports 29 states and up to $16.68B against Meta's own 52 attorneys general and about $18.59B); appeal deadlines were not found. Governance facts come from the 2026 proxy (read through a mirror) and press reports opened Nov 12.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001326801/000162828026066773/meta-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://investor.atmeta.com/investor-news/press-release-details/2026/Meta-Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Results/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Q3 release</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001326801/000162828026066700/meta-09302026xexhibit991.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Q3 release on SEC, Class C terms</a> · <a href=\"https://s21.q4cdn.com/399680738/files/content_files/META-Q3-2026-Earnings-Call-Transcript.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">company transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.boardroomalpha.com/sec/meta-def-14a-2026-04-16-0001628280-26-025532\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2026 proxy, mirror</a> · <a href=\"https://thedeepdive.ca/meta-calls-25-billion-new-mexico-judgment-a-tax-on-speech-vows-appeal/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Deep Dive, New Mexico judgment</a> · <a href=\"https://www.pymnts.com/legal/2026/meta-slams-new-mexico-business-climate-after-25-billion-verdict/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PYMNTS</a> · <a href=\"https://www.drugwatch.com/social-media-addiction/lawsuit/timeline/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Drugwatch timeline</a> · <a href=\"https://techpolicy.press